steps.prompt:
Inspect all input files staged in $FLEET_INPUT_DIR/example/ and read the task carefully:

${example.prompt}

Implement the required solution cleanly, verify your changes with the appropriate local tools/runtime, and write all modified or newly created deliverable files directly into $FLEET_OUTPUT_DIR (preserving their expected relative paths). Also write a concise summary in $FLEET_OUTPUT_DIR/output.json.

Review the implementation in $FLEET_INPUT_DIR/implement/ against the original inputs in $FLEET_INPUT_DIR/example/ and the task requirements:

${example.prompt}

Check correctness, edge cases, contract adherence, code quality and missing deliverables. Review the staged files without editing them. Return one JSON object as your final reply, without code fences. Include "verdict" as a nonempty string, "findings" as an array of concrete finding strings (empty if there are none), and "report" as the full Markdown report in a JSON string. Fleet retains the report and summary for the fix step.

Read the original inputs in $FLEET_INPUT_DIR/example/, the initial implementation in $FLEET_INPUT_DIR/implement/, and the review findings in $FLEET_INPUT_DIR/review/ for the task:

${example.prompt}

Address every valid review finding, verify the final deliverables cleanly, and write all final deliverable files (copying any unchanged deliverables from $FLEET_INPUT_DIR/implement/ and updating changed ones) into $FLEET_OUTPUT_DIR (preserving their expected relative paths), plus a concise summary in $FLEET_OUTPUT_DIR/output.json.
